description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, localize the drafter grounding window by SYMBOL when the gap carries no line number, porting the fallback that goal-host-vessel already uses.

WHY (measured): of 368 code-edit specs, 88 percent name a bare file path with no location inside the file, so startLine stays 0 and the drafter receives lines 1 to 40 of a file that can be 11645 lines long. The goal-host edit-intent path already solves this in verbatimExcerptBlock, which when no line is given picks the first identifier named in the goal text that appears in a declaration position in the file and windows there, labelling it around symbol X. Autonomous gap pickup has no such fallback. Reuse that idea here rather than inventing a new one.

Replace this line, which occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file (this is your verbatim anchor):
          const from = Math.max(0, startLine - 15);

with exactly these two lines:
          if (startLine === 0) { const toks = Array.from(new Set(String(summary).split(" ").map((w) => w.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_]/g, "")).filter((w) => w.length > 5))); for (const id of toks) { const hit = liveLines.findIndex((l) => l.includes("function " + id) || l.includes("const " + id) || l.includes(id + "(")); if (hit >= 0) { startLine = hit + 1; console.log("[gap-to-feature] symbol->line: " + id + " grounds " + firstTarget + " at line " + startLine); break; } } }
          const from: number = Math.max(0, startLine - 15);

NOTES ON SCOPE. summary is declared earlier in this same function as const summary = String(gap.summary ?? gap.title ?? ""); and is a string. liveLines, startLine, and firstTarget are all already in scope at this point; startLine is a let. The existing region-based fallback just above is left untouched and still takes precedence.

CONSTRAINTS. Exactly one edit op on that one line. Do not add a helper function, do not add imports, do not change any other line. It must typecheck with no new errors.

